menu "Errors"

    config ERRORS_INFO
        bool "Record where errors are created"
        default y
        help
          Store the place an error was created: the source file name
          (__FILE_NAME__, without the path), the line and the function. One
          record per call site, in flash; the node points to it. Costs one
          string per source file and per function that creates errors, in
          flash. When off, error nodes have no `info` field at all.

    config ERRORS_POOL_BLOCKS
        int "Error pool: number of blocks"
        default 32
        range 4 255
        help
          How many error nodes can exist at once (one node = one block).
          RAM used = ERRORS_POOL_BLOCKS * ERRORS_POOL_BLOCK_SIZE.

    config ERRORS_POOL_BLOCK_SIZE
        int "Error pool: block size (bytes)"
        default 32
        range 16 128
        help
          Size of one block = node header (12 B with info, 8 B without) +
          largest payload. Must be a multiple of 4.

    config ERRORS_LOG_LINE_LEN
        int "Error log: line buffer size (bytes)"
        default 256
        range 64 512
        help
          Size of the stack buffer err_log() formats one chain node into.
          Longer lines are cut.

    config ERRORS_RECORD_REQ_MAX
        int "Request bytes kept in an error record"
        default 32
        range 0 127
        help
          How much of the failing request (keys + payload) an error record
          repeats. Longer requests are cut and marked.

    config ERRORS_MAX_MODULES
        int "Maximum error modules"
        default 32
        range 1 255
        help
          How many modules can register an error tag table
          (ERR_MODULE_DEFINE). One pointer of RAM per slot.

endmenu
